{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Reload",
  "description": "A service pistol reloaded in a quiet room, close to the microphone: dry, dense, damped clacks with steel sliding between them, nothing that rings. A full magazine rasps up the magazine well and seats, the catch snapping over it just after, with the palm's thump on the polymer grip behind both. A pause, then the slide is racked back, a 'shh' of steel on steel with the rails' machining ticking under it, slowing as the spring loads, and knocks its rear stop. Let go, the slide runs home, the loudest hit: slide meeting barrel, then the lock-up right after, a chunky double clack with the frame's knock under it and the recoil spring chattering for a moment after.",
  "tags": [
    "weapon",
    "gun",
    "reload",
    "click",
    "pistol",
    "magazine",
    "slide",
    "rack",
    "mechanical",
    "foley"
  ],
  "duration": "auto",
  "seed": 7,
  "tracks": [
